Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.24.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.24.0: after hosting, the app content fills the whole window so the user's finger lands on the app and the move gesture never triggers (archive 26: move works in the picker page, dead after hosting). Fix: invisible 16 pt edge strips are added on the left and right so the window can be grabbed from any of the four edges; the right strip stops 70 pt above the bottom to keep the corner exclusively for the resize grip. App picking now lists ALL installed apps (LSApplicationWorkspace allInstalledApplications): running apps get a dot prefix and sort first, not-running ones sort by name, and tapping a not-running app launches it through FBSOpenApplicationService (in-process SpringBoard, respondsToSelector + try/catch guarded) and auto-hosts it 2 s later when the scene exists (openOrHostBundleID). The defaultBundleID auto-host path uses the same launch-then-host route. No new config keys; cfgVersion stays 20.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
